# What git tracks in this project, by way of what it does not.
#
# The Markdown, the class file, figures/*.svg and the scripts are sources.
# Everything else is produced by running them, and is left out so that a
# clone is the source and a checkout never carries a stale build.
#
# figures/*.svg is written by the drawing scripts but is tracked: it is what
# the documents reference and what the archive ships.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the PDFs
# Every document keeps its generated LaTeX, LaTeX's scratch files and its PDF
# beside its Markdown: in src/ for the lectures, in a course-year folder such
# as 2026/ for homework and exams. Those are named here rather than the
# folders, since the folders also hold the sources. buildtex.py also writes
# a PDF beside each figure's SVG.
src/*.tex
src/*.pdf
20[0-9][0-9]/*.tex
20[0-9][0-9]/*.pdf
figures/*.pdf

# LaTeX's scratch files, and the MathML copy the tagging code writes beside
# each PDF
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz
*-luamml-mathml.html

# ------------------------------------------------------------- the website
/web/
/site/

# ------------------------------------------------------------- the archive
/{{ARCHIVE}}.zip

# --------------------------------------------------- the originals and scratch
# originals/ holds the files the transcription is made from, and work/ the
# page images rendered from them. No script reads either. Delete the
# /originals/ line to keep the originals in the repository: adding them later
# is one commit, removing them later means rewriting history.
/originals/
/work/

